@startuml
title System Component Overview

component "Motherboard" as MB
component "CPU\n(1024-bit asm model)" as CPU
component "GPU\n(1024-bit asm model)" as GPU
component "RAM" as RAM
component "Firmware / ROM" as ROM
component "Storage" as STO
component "Chipset / I-O Hub" as CHIP
component "Power Delivery" as PWR
component "Cooling" as COOL
component "PCIe / Expansion" as PCIE

MB o-- CPU : socket/package
MB o-- GPU : slot/package
MB o-- RAM : memory channels
MB o-- ROM : boot firmware
MB o-- STO : persistent data
MB o-- CHIP : board I/O
MB o-- PWR : voltage regulation
MB o-- COOL : thermal management
MB o-- PCIE : expansion bus

CPU --> RAM : loads/stores
GPU --> RAM : shared buffers
CPU --> GPU : command stream
GPU --> CPU : results / interrupts
ROM --> CPU : boot code
STO --> RAM : program/data load
CHIP --> STO : storage controller
CHIP --> PCIE : peripheral routing

note right of MB
The current assembly project models
CPU/GPU state and a simplified memory
stream, not a full motherboard.
end note

@enduml
